    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Tracks how many TTS samples the audio device has actually consumed, so consumers pacing work against playback (e.g. lip sync) can slave to it. Safe to query from any thread; the speaker updates it on the game thread. Samples queued to a procedural sound that was discarded before draining (format change, EndPlay) count as played. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
